{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-fable-5-1","id":"msg_011CfUmcQiLzbgbNA12nGCan","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01B2aVQuQNdbyb5HMSA29Nt1","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cat > /tmp/it8/sec35_tail.md <<'EOF'\n\n**Finding, in one paragraph.** Between 75 and 100 customers the `m = n`\nridge's rate did not keep falling. Read as what they are — one exact count\nand a cell of censored lower bounds — the 100 cell's location implies a\nrate of {{R_PRE}} log10 per customer over 75 → 100 under pre-fix `csearch`\nand {{R_DEF}} under `default`, against 0.092–0.095 over 60 → 75 and 0.085–0.089\nhad §16's drift continued; the quadratic's curvature on 10–100 is no longer\nnegative ({{CURV}}) and on 40–100 it is positive, so the law is **not\nsub-exponential** on the ridge — the power law loses to the exponential by\nover a thousand AIC in every series — and the drift §16 pooled from 18\nseries does **not saturate on the ridge, it reverses**, while on the `d = 4`\nneighbour, where the 100 cell is five instances, the negative curvature\nsurvives (−5.4 × 10⁻⁵ `default`, −2.8 × 10⁻⁵ pre-fix `csearch`). Compared like\nwith like — pre-fix `csearch` law against pre-fix `csearch` record — the\nconstant-rate exponential refitted on 10–100 puts the median\n`Random-125-125-2` refutation at **{{E125}} log10 nodes [{{E125_BAND}}]** with\nthe record's three counts at 11.21, 11.22 and 11.66 (a spread of one\ninstance, σ₁₀₀ ≈ 0.5, around it), where §16(e)'s drifting figure of 11.00 sat\n0.2 below the record and its `default` figure of 11.18 was never comparable;\nthe pointwise reading that carries the 75 → 100 rise to 125 gives\n**{{L125}}**, which the record contradicts by 0.8–1.2 decades. So either the\nrise is confined to the 75–100 interval — the three 125 counts say the rate\nover 100 → 125 is back near {{R_REC}} — or the generated ridge at `col_mean`\n3.04 is harder at 125 than the corpus class at 2.76, which the 100-customer\ncorpus counts (≥ 9.31–9.42 censored, 7.97 and 8.27 settled, against the\ncell's ≥ 9.25–9.35 and 9.00–9.29) do not suggest; the `d = 4` analogue's\nrecord (10.69, 10.78, 11.41) sits 0.4–0.7 *below* its exponential refit and on\n§16's drifting figure. **The revised law, stated once:** on the ridge, pre-fix\n`csearch`, `log10 nodes = {{A_PRE}} + {{B_PRE}} n` from 10 to 100 with no\nresolvable drift, σ growing to 0.5 at 100; at 125 a median of\n**{{E125_NODES}} nodes ({{E125_LO_NODES}} to {{E125_HI_NODES}} on the median;\n×/÷ 7 for one instance)**, {{E125_H}} hours per refutation on one core at\n1.4 × 10⁶ nodes/s, against 25–72 hours spent on the record. Post-fix, the\nsame refutations cost the fix ratio more: {{FIX_RATIO}} on the 100 cell\n(one exact pair at 2.15, the rest lower bounds), ≥ 19.6 on\n`Random-100-100-2-4_0` (§31). **For re-certifying the withdrawn instances**:\nthe two still open (`Random-125-125-2-2_0`, `-2-3_0`, running since\n2026-09-24 on the pre-fix library with five-day budgets) are priced by this\nlaw at a median of {{E125_H}} h with a factor-7 instance spread, so the\nfive-day budget covers the median and not the tail; and re-refuting all\neight 125 × 125 instances on the fixed code — the six on record carry the\npre-fix caveat — costs at least {{FIX_RATIO}} × that, a median of\n{{POST_H}} hours ({{POST_D}} days) per instance on one core, two to four\ncore-weeks in all, with the `d = 2` tail (`-2-5_0` took 72 h pre-fix) at a\nfortnight or more. That is the price of a clean corpus at 125 × 125, and it\nis a `csearch`-configuration price: `default` at 125 is 11.7–11.8 by the same\nrefit and has no count on record.\n\n**Size range covered.** Generated `m = n` fixed-`d` instances at 10–100\ncustomers: `d = 3` at 10–75 fully certified (150 per cell to 40, 50 above),\nat 100 the 24 instances of §34's cell that survive the pre-fix check (1\ncertified, 23 verified upper bounds with censored steps; pre-fix `csearch`\n{{PRE_SETTLED}} settled of 24); `d = 4` at 100 on §16(d)'s five (1 certified). Chu &\nStuckey's `Random-100-100-2/4` and `Random-125-125-2/4` enter only as the\nrecord. **Every 125 figure is an extrapolation of 25 customers** from a cell\nthat is itself mostly lower bounds, and rests on the reading that a value\nthe descent reached in 2,400 s is optimal — one of 25 was not.\n\n**Kill criterion.** The plan states none for item 08. Its deliverable — the\nrevised law and its band, and a sentence on the withdrawn instances — is the\nparagraph above.\n\n**Method notes.** (1) *A censored cell has a location, not a median*: the\ncensored median of the 100 cell (≥ 9.5–9.6) understates its centre by\n0.5–0.8 decades under any normal reading with the 75 cell's spread; §34's\n\"≥ 9.64\" was right and was not the centre. (2) *Read the pre-fix record\nwith a pre-fix law*: §16(e)'s headline match used the `default` law; the\n`csearch` row of its own table sat 0.2 below the record, which is where the\nrefit lands it. (3) *Ask the satisfiable side at 100 too*: one pre-fix call\nlowered a value the post-fix descent had left standing after 2,400 s, and\nits censored counts had been entering §34's cell summary as refutation\nbounds. (4) *`spawn` cannot re-import a stdin script*: a pool launched from\n`python -` respawned failing workers into a 40 MB log until killed by PID;\nlaunch pools from a file. (5) Seconds here are from a machine at load 37–42\n(28 foreign workers and 8 recertify workers beside these 16): 0.8–0.9 × 10⁶\nnodes/s, so 2,400 s censored at ≈ 2 × 10⁹ nodes; nodes are the claim.\nEOF\ncd /home/al/dev/MOSP && for i in $(seq 1 100); do n=$(wc -l < learning/data/ensemble/ridge100_prefix_calls.csv); if [ \"$n\" -ge 26 ] || grep -q \"wall:\" learning/data/ensemble/ridge100_prefix_run.log; then break; fi; sleep 6; done; date; tail -5 learning/data/ensemble/ridge100_prefix_run.log","description":"Draft the finding and method notes, then wait up to ten minutes for the pre-fix run to complete","timeout":620000},"calle