{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-fable-5-1","id":"msg_011CfUqSXCDPhma554E5iuFM","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Item 08 is complete: the report section, tables, data, tests, PROGRESS entry and iterations mark are all written, the full suite passes, and nothing under `solutions/` changed.\n\n**What was done**\n\n- **Like-with-like comparison established first.** The six 125 × 125 recertify counts and every campaign `csearch` count below 100 customers are pre-fix numbers, while §34's 100-cell `csearch` counts are post-fix. To compare fairly, I ran the pre-fix `csearch` rule (item 04's `prefix` variant) on all 25 ridge-100 instances at `value − 1`. 15.2 core-hours on 16 workers. Result: 5 refuted (log10 nodes 9.00–9.29), 19 censored at ≥ 9.25–9.35, and one `sat`: `i005`'s value 26 was not optimal (now 25, witness saved under the ensemble directory). That instance leaves every series at 100 since its censored counts bounded a witness search.\n- **Refit as a Tobit** (`learning/rate_drift.py`): censored maximum likelihood for four law shapes with a size-dependent scale, on 10–100 and 40–100, bootstrap bands, plus the 100 cell's censored-normal location.\n\n**Findings** (`reports/ml_nature.md` §35, `reports/rate_drift_tables.md`)\n\n- **The rate did not keep falling.** Over 75 → 100 the cell's location implies 0.116 [0.110, 0.121] per customer under pre-fix `csearch` and 0.140 under `default`, against 0.092–0.095 over 60 → 75. The quadratic curvature flips from negative on 10–75 to positive with the cell. Not sub-exponential (the power law loses by over 1,000 AIC everywhere). The drift reverses on the ridge and survives only on the d = 4 neighbour.\n- **At 125, like with like:** the exponential refit gives 11.43 [11.36, 11.51] with the record (11.21, 11.22, 11.66) 0.2 either side. §16(e)'s drifting `csearch` figure of 11.00 sat 0.22 below; its headline 11.18 was a `default` figure. Readings that carry the 75 → 100 rise forward (12.4–12.6) are contradicted by the record by 0.8–1.4 decades, so the rise is not sustained to 125 in the corpus class.\n- **Revised law:** `log10 nodes = −0.24 + 0.0934 n`, median 2.7 × 10¹¹ nodes at 125, 55 h per refutation on one core pre-fix. Fix ratio on the 100 cell ≥ 2.34× (one exact pair at 2.15). Re-refuting the eight 125 × 125 instances on the fixed code costs ≥ 130 h per instance median, about six core-weeks.\n\n**Tests:** `tests/test_rate_drift.py` (8 tests). Full suite 1,178 passed, 2 skipped, 1 xfailed in 440 s on a loaded machine.\n\n**Caveats noted in the report:** 19 of 24 pre-fix calls censored because the machine ran at load 37–42 (28 foreign workers appeared mid-session), so the pre-fix cell rests on the 75 cell's spread; pre-fix `unsat` answers are refutations under the over-pruning rule, not certificates."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":32,"cache_creation_input_tokens":250200,"cache_read_input_tokens":10243,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":250200,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":816,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"9aa8bc60-cd4b-49b2-a521-0ca5d75d3528","uuid":"2fb28546-8635-4fba-be2c-2602bbf331e8","timestamp":"2026-09-27T23:46:57.280Z","request_id":"req_011CfUqSVS3LxJCq57wmT6sg"}
